[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The reports merged into
it show three problems. Each has its own ticket now, with the number of reports it covers.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first row. The form hint and the one-day move stay broken
after it ships.
</Callout>

## What the reports show

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

- **`parser`**: the tenant writes the day first and the shared parser reads the month first.
  7 April goes out as 4 July. Every tenant in #4471 is affected, on every channel.
- **`hint`**: only on booking-v3 tenants, only through the form. The form tells people to type
  `MM/DD/YYYY` and then reads what they typed day first. Same symptom, different code.
- **`one-day`**: the date is right, the day is not. "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in
  Toronto got Monday." "Only June." No day/month pair in these reports swaps. The desk noted
  them in `desk-notes.json`; the #4471 page files them under `parser` by tenant, as a footnote.
  The last one says the reporter stopped reporting these, so this count is a floor.

## How they were told apart

- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, so ids are counted once.
- The cause follows the tenant (`causes.ts`), not intake's tag. Intake guesses from the
  reporter's browser and disagrees with the tenant often.
- The subject line says nothing about the cause. Subjects repeat across all three problems, so
  [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merged them into one ticket.

## For the desk

- Before you merge a report into #4471, check which problem it shows. A one-day move goes to its
  own ticket, a booking-v3 form report goes to the hint ticket.
- Decision 0001 is accepted and stays as written. Merging on subject alone is what hid these
  problems; it needs a new decision record.

